FIX-115 measured the collector on deployment 6d1650a4: longest GC pause of any
minute 148 ms. The ~13 s blocks are not garbage collection. The watchdog took
one stack at 5 s and the next at 35 s and never said how long a stall lasted.

- lib/main-thread-watchdog.js: sample every 3 s while stalled (at most 5 per
  stall); print `MAIN THREAD RESUMED after N.Ns (k samples)` on return.
- tape/run.js: `TAPE TURN` — how many venue messages were dispatched in ONE
  turn of the loop and how long it took (written when >= 1 s), and a one-line
  minute summary with the slowest single message. A backlog and a slow message
  are fixed differently; from outside they look the same. Re-pinned (SCOPE-5).
- learning/service.js: `LEARNING STEP <label> held the main lane Nms` for any
  measured step >= 1 s (the meter existed; the log never named it).

Diagnostics only, authority NONE, no frozen byte.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
